\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Experiment 2: EADD vs.\ D3 on the four annotated real-world datasets. Prec.\ = Precision; Rec.\ = Recall on known drift points; MTD = Mean Time to Detection (samples; lower is better). Bold indicates EADD outperforms D3. ``---'' = all known drift points missed. Low precision on incremental datasets reflects the INSECTS annotation convention: only major transition boundaries are annotated; additional detections may correspond to unannotated continuous incremental changes rather than false alarms. Data from \texttt  {experiment2\_realworld.csv}.}}{56}{table.caption.103}\protected@file@percent }
